0030 — TRI and TEX_TRI draw a pixel on a shared edge once.

Both triangle rasterisers counted a pixel centre exactly on an edge as
inside (`w >= 0` on all three edge functions), so a centre on an edge two
triangles share was drawn by both. Every image under a perspective root is
TEX_TRI cells, two triangles a cell, cells sharing edges; every turned
two-stop gradient is a TRI fan. Under a translucent fill the shared edge
was blended twice: a dark disc at 82 % alpha over a bright ground showed a
darker line along its cells' diagonal — a full line where the diagonal runs
at 45 degrees through pixel centres, dashed at any other scale.

Now each edge owns the centres exactly on it only when it runs down the
screen or, level, leftward (`edge_min`). Two positively wound triangles
traverse a shared edge in opposite directions, and exactly one of a
direction and its negation qualifies, so a centre on a shared edge is drawn
by exactly one of them. Coverage everywhere else is unchanged, and so are
the barycentric weights.

Class `upstream`: the rule belongs to the software rasteriser upstream
ships as much as to this one, with no target-side cost — as `0021`. Not
run: upstream's PNG goldens, which need its sim prep builds (as at the pin
move). A centre exactly on an outer edge that does not own it is no longer
drawn — half the edge directions — so a rotated image or gradient whose
outer edge runs through pixel centres can lose those pixels.

Guard: `a_translucent_image_in_perspective_draws_each_pixel_once`
(`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): a uniform half-alpha black texture as an
Image under `perspective` 2600 over white — flat at z 0 and -300, and
turned 30 degrees about Y — shows one colour; so does a turned box whose
two-stop gradient is one translucent colour (a TRI fan). Red before (z 0:
two colours, the diagonal blended twice), green after.

The film it was found in (`mg-hud`, frame 40, its 540 px disc PNG at alpha
209 under `perspective-[2600]`): rendered with and without this patch, the
1 px 45-degree line across the disc is gone; the other changed pixels are
the 6 px dot images' own edges, spread by the glow layer they sit in.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: no digest and no
`visibility` row moves — no ledger composition draws an image in
perspective, and none puts a TRI or TEX_TRI edge through a pixel centre.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

