+/// The smallest edge-function value at which a pixel centre counts as inside
+/// the edge a -> b of a positively wound triangle: 0 when the edge owns the
+/// centres lying exactly on it, 1 when it does not. Two triangles sharing an
+/// edge traverse it in opposite directions, and exactly one of a direction
+/// and its negation runs down the screen or, level, leftward — so a centre on
+/// a shared edge is drawn once. Inclusive on every edge, it was drawn by both,
+/// and under a translucent fill (a dark disc at 82 % alpha) the shared
+/// diagonal of every TEX_TRI pair was a darker line (pocket-motion patch 0030).
+#[inline]
+fn edge_min(ax: i64, ay: i64, bx: i64, by: i64) -> i64 {
+    let (dx, dy) = (bx - ax, by - ay);
+    if dy > 0 || (dy == 0 && dx < 0) {
+        0
+    } else {
+        1
+    }
+}
